+# Corpus fetching
+
+The corpus fetch ran under Svipall's per-domain limit of **12 visits per
+60-second window**. Breaching that limit imposed a **900-second (15-minute)
+cooldown** for the affected domain. In practice, fetches were therefore made in
+batches of no more than 12 visits per domain, with at least 65 seconds between
+batches.
+
+Files were fetched through these CDN or mirror hosts:
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com`
+- `cdn.jsdelivr.net` (using `/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<branch>/<path>` URLs)
+- `cdn.statically.io` (this mirror was slow and sometimes timed out)
+
+The corpus manifest independently identifies `raw.githubusercontent.com` as the
+raw-file source. The exact limit, cooldown, batching interval, and alternate
+mirrors are preserved in the project's corpus-fetch session record; no fetch
+script or request log containing those details is checked into this checkout.
